STYLE: A grand hand-made toy theatre production built from printed card. Every piece is a flat cutout of thick card about 4 mm thick, cut by hand with a craft knife. The front of each piece is painted in the manner of an Italian maritime ex-voto of the 1800s: naive, earnest tempera on a small wooden panel, flat clear colour with simple modelling, precise little boats and rigging, curling stylised waves with white crests, sturdy fisherfolk with simple dignified faces, varnish cracks and a soft warm patina of age. Bold, clear shapes that read from the back row. Puppet joints are brass split pins. Palette: limewash white #EFE7D6, sea green #2F5E5A, deep sea #1C3442, storm slate #4C5662, terracotta #B4593A, ochre #C8963E, faded red #9C3B2E, sail cream #E8DCC0, with raw card brown #A57E52 at cut edges. The mood is grief, endurance and work by the sea.
CONSTRAINTS: No text, no letters, no numbers, no "PGR", no signature, no watermark. No religious figures, no saints, no Madonna, no crosses, no halos, no angels. No flags. No photographic people, no 3D render look, no plastic, no glossy finish, no anime style.
REFERENCES: Image 1 is the look reference. Match its naive ex-voto tempera, flat colour, curling waves, varnish patina, palette, raw card edges and figure style. Do not copy its composition.
SUBJECT: The four pieces of a marionette of Matteo, a strong Italian fisherman and stonemason of about forty, facing three-quarters to the right: (1) the head with dark curly hair greying at the temples, a full moustache, a weathered steady face, and the bare neck; (2) the body from the neck base down to heavy boots, in a white shirt with rolled sleeves, a brown wool waistcoat, a red sash at the waist, dark trousers, standing, with NO arms; (3) his RIGHT arm from shoulder to a strong hand closed in a grip, as if on a rope or a wheel handle, white rolled sleeve; (4) his LEFT arm from shoulder to an open hand, white rolled sleeve.
COMPOSITION: A flat lay of the separate cardboard pieces of ONE jointed puppet, all at the same scale, seen straight from the front on a transparent background. Each piece is a separate cutout with clear empty space around it. No piece touches or overlaps another piece. No shadow, no rod, no strings, no stand, no stage.
JOINTS: The body has three clearly visible round brass split pins: one at the centre of the base of the neck and one on each shoulder. The body ends at the neck base with no head and has no arms. The head piece ends in a bare neck with no collar, with one brass pin at the bottom of the neck. Each arm piece has one brass pin at the very top of the shoulder. One arm is a RIGHT arm and the other is a LEFT arm, each hanging straight down from its shoulder pin, with the thumbs on the correct sides. The head is drawn at a natural size for the body.
